  "text": "proprium.dominica-xix-post-pentecosten-epistola",
  "about": "The epistola of the formulary “19th Sunday after Pentecost” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Brethren: Be renewed in the spirit of your mind, and clothe yourselves with the new man, who was created according to God in justice and in the holiness of truth. Therefore, laying aside falsehood, speak the truth, each one with his neighbor, since we are members one of another. Be angry, and do not sin; do not let the sun set upon your anger. Do not give place to the devil. Let the one who was stealing steal no more, but rather let him toil, doing what is good with his own hands, so that he may have the means to give to one who suffers want." }
  },
